1
00:00:13,888 --> 00:00:16,933
OUR STICKY LOVE

2
00:00:38,204 --> 00:00:39,873
After everything today,

3
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:43,918
you must be tired. When we get home,
wash up and get some sleep.

4
00:00:47,047 --> 00:00:50,508
Yeah, I'll get some sleep, but…

5
00:00:54,929 --> 00:00:56,973
Speaking of sleep…

6
00:01:01,853 --> 00:01:03,688
When will we start sharing a room again?

7
00:01:05,190 --> 00:01:06,191
What?

8
00:01:06,941 --> 00:01:10,486
I believe that you're my boyfriend now.

9
00:01:10,487 --> 00:01:12,447
I have no choice but to,

10
00:01:13,990 --> 00:01:17,327
and I think I've figured out
why I fell for you.

11
00:01:21,206 --> 00:01:25,501
I know you're being considerate
because I lost my memory,

12
00:01:25,502 --> 00:01:28,338
but what if my memory never returns?

13
00:01:30,256 --> 00:01:33,051
Will we sleep in separate rooms forever?

14
00:01:33,927 --> 00:01:36,304
Like we're just housemates?

15
00:01:44,854 --> 00:01:47,941
I'm saying we should start
getting back to normal.

16
00:01:48,525 --> 00:01:50,693
Our plans to get married,

17
00:01:51,277 --> 00:01:52,570
and that we were in love…

18
00:01:54,572 --> 00:01:55,907
I believe it all.

19
00:01:58,201 --> 00:02:00,286
I guess I'm trying to say…

20
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:07,168
I'd be open to sharing a room

21
00:02:08,169 --> 00:02:09,379
now that I trust you.

22
00:02:18,513 --> 00:02:20,265
Do I need to keep going?

23
00:02:30,316 --> 00:02:32,694
The thing is…

24
00:02:36,823 --> 00:02:40,535
I don't think… we can do that right now.

25
00:02:42,453 --> 00:02:43,371
Why not?

26
00:02:44,247 --> 00:02:46,166
A pleasure to meet you, ma'am!

27
00:02:49,836 --> 00:02:54,257
I'm Kim Gang-rok, Tae-ha's junior.

28
00:02:56,301 --> 00:02:59,720
He came here to settle down
but hasn't found a place yet.

29
00:02:59,721 --> 00:03:01,514
And as you can see, his foot's hurt.

30
00:03:03,141 --> 00:03:06,227
So he's staying here with us
until he finds a place?

31
00:03:07,353 --> 00:03:09,730
Yes, I'll only be here for a little while.

32
00:03:09,731 --> 00:03:13,567
Just think of me as your little brother.
I'm at your disposal, whatever you need.

33
00:03:13,568 --> 00:03:17,821
Yeah, and he'll be sharing my room,
so you don't have to worry about a thing.

34
00:03:17,822 --> 00:03:19,114
Yes, I'll be… What?

35
00:03:19,115 --> 00:03:20,408
- What?
- What?

36
00:03:23,203 --> 00:03:25,996
Wouldn't it be better
if you two shared a room

37
00:03:25,997 --> 00:03:28,457
and I slept in a different room?

38
00:03:28,458 --> 00:03:29,834
I think so too.

39
00:03:33,421 --> 00:03:37,508
Still, you're a guest.
It'd be impolite to make you sleep alone.

40
00:03:38,801 --> 00:03:40,428
Since when is that impolite?

41
00:03:41,846 --> 00:03:44,724
Maybe he'll carry you on his back
and sing you a lullaby too.

42
00:03:50,730 --> 00:03:53,565
I don't want to rush into
sharing a room either,

43
00:03:53,566 --> 00:03:55,068
so let's do that, then.

44
00:03:55,568 --> 00:03:57,403
You should sleep with him.

45
00:03:57,904 --> 00:03:58,947
Politely.

46
00:03:59,530 --> 00:04:01,114
Okay, thanks.

47
00:04:01,115 --> 00:04:02,116
"Thanks"?

48
00:04:08,456 --> 00:04:09,374
"Thanks"?

49
00:04:12,543 --> 00:04:14,295
Have a good night's…

50
00:04:17,715 --> 00:04:18,674
Sir!

51
00:04:18,675 --> 00:04:19,925
What? What is it?

52
00:04:19,926 --> 00:04:23,262
Who does he think he is?
Some kind of saint? Confucian scholar?

53
00:04:23,263 --> 00:04:27,058
Why is he so big on politeness,
making sure his guest sleeps well?

54
00:04:30,687 --> 00:04:31,896
So annoying.

55
00:04:36,567 --> 00:04:39,654
Why did I have to bring up sharing a room?

56
00:04:40,446 --> 00:04:43,116
This is so humiliating.

57
00:04:44,659 --> 00:04:47,412
What the heck is wrong with him?

58
00:04:48,746 --> 00:04:49,580
I mean…

59
00:04:50,164 --> 00:04:53,125
I thought you were
supposed to be her boyfriend.

60
00:04:53,126 --> 00:04:56,211
Shouldn't you share a room
with Prosecutor Go to really sell it?

61
00:04:56,212 --> 00:04:57,671
Just lay out the bedding.

62
00:04:57,672 --> 00:05:00,882
I don't understand you. Not one bit.

63
00:05:00,883 --> 00:05:05,429
Putting the act aside,
you like Prosecutor Go, right?

64
00:05:05,430 --> 00:05:08,682
Then, of course,
you should share a room with her.

65
00:05:08,683 --> 00:05:09,767
Why insist on…

66
00:05:13,354 --> 00:05:14,314
Hold up.

67
00:05:16,190 --> 00:05:17,275
Are you shy?

68
00:05:21,237 --> 00:05:22,363
How cute.

69
00:05:24,949 --> 00:05:29,619
I know you're hopeless
when it comes to women,

70
00:05:29,620 --> 00:05:33,458
but I didn't know
you were such a teenager.

71
00:05:36,377 --> 00:05:39,589
Are you not mentally prepared
to share a room just yet?

72
00:05:43,384 --> 00:05:46,346
Is your heart pounding
because she's your first love?

73
00:05:48,222 --> 00:05:50,098
How exactly do you feel?

74
00:05:50,099 --> 00:05:52,100
Are your nerves getting to you?

75
00:05:52,101 --> 00:05:54,353
I wouldn't know. God, this is killing me.

76
00:05:54,354 --> 00:05:55,772
Seriously, I wouldn't know.

77
00:05:56,356 --> 00:05:57,190
Oh, my stomach.

78
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:03,488
Do you want to be shaking with fear?
All over?

79
00:06:04,447 --> 00:06:05,615
I'm sorry.

80
00:06:10,870 --> 00:06:11,704
Well,

81
00:06:12,497 --> 00:06:14,374
good night.

82
00:06:20,505 --> 00:06:21,339
But, sir.

83
00:06:22,090 --> 00:06:25,008
Now that she's back,
what are you going to do?

84
00:06:25,009 --> 00:06:27,303
I heard you'll be smuggling her
out of the country.

85
00:06:34,143 --> 00:06:35,394
How do you know that?

86
00:06:35,395 --> 00:06:38,730
When you were busy looking for her,
I asked Mr. Hong.

87
00:06:38,731 --> 00:06:41,692
I knew you wouldn't have saved her
without a plan.

88
00:06:47,115 --> 00:06:48,574
The boat leaves late this month.

89
00:06:51,285 --> 00:06:52,494
Late this month?

90
00:06:52,495 --> 00:06:53,870
I'll send her off then.

91
00:06:53,871 --> 00:06:55,997
If her memory returns by then,

92
00:06:55,998 --> 00:06:58,750
I'm sure she'll leave willingly
to avoid Chairman Baek.

93
00:06:58,751 --> 00:07:00,336
But what if it doesn't?

94
00:07:03,881 --> 00:07:06,675
Then I'll have to force her
to leave the country.

95
00:07:06,676 --> 00:07:08,428
That's the only way she'll be safe.

96
00:07:10,930 --> 00:07:15,350
And let's not call her Prosecutor Go
in this house, even if it's just us.

97
00:07:15,351 --> 00:07:17,937
If she finds out before she remembers,
she'll be at risk.

98
00:07:18,771 --> 00:07:20,440
Yes, understood.

99
00:07:21,899 --> 00:07:22,733
Good night.

100
00:07:30,741 --> 00:07:32,659
Please go on and get some sleep.

101
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:34,578
I'll be back after a quick smoke.

102
00:07:34,579 --> 00:07:35,621
Okay.

103
00:07:40,168 --> 00:07:41,586
I'll turn off the lights.

104
00:08:21,459 --> 00:08:23,044
Come have breakfast!

105
00:08:25,963 --> 00:08:27,756
You cooked all this by yourself?

106
00:08:27,757 --> 00:08:31,760
I didn't know what you'd like,
so I prepared a variety of cuisines,

107
00:08:31,761 --> 00:08:34,137
from Asia to the Middle East
and even the US.

108
00:08:34,138 --> 00:08:37,016
You won't have to worry about meals
while I'm here.

109
00:08:39,936 --> 00:08:40,937
- Let's eat.
- Okay.

110
00:08:41,521 --> 00:08:42,480
Enjoy your meal!

111
00:08:43,564 --> 00:08:44,565
Looks good.

112
00:08:48,069 --> 00:08:48,985
Of course.

113
00:08:48,986 --> 00:08:51,154
I knew you'd go for that first.

114
00:08:51,155 --> 00:08:54,074
I made this for him all the time
when he was hungover.

115
00:08:54,075 --> 00:08:56,452
His gochujang stew is great.
You should try it.

116
00:08:58,996 --> 00:09:00,706
I don't really like gochujang.

117
00:09:01,541 --> 00:09:02,999
- I'll have this.
- Sure.

118
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:05,877
Whatever you eat,
just eat a lot and get better.

119
00:09:05,878 --> 00:09:08,548
- And I hope your clinic visit goes well.
- Clinic visit?

120
00:09:09,549 --> 00:09:12,051
Don't you get treatment
on Tuesdays and Fridays?

121
00:09:13,052 --> 00:09:14,720
Did Mr. Hong tell you that too?

122
00:09:16,264 --> 00:09:19,516
I've been your right-hand man
for ten years now.

123
00:09:19,517 --> 00:09:21,978
Keeping tabs on your schedule is a given.

124
00:09:23,229 --> 00:09:28,234
Eat up, and good luck
with your treatment today.

125
00:09:39,161 --> 00:09:40,829
If I remember correctly,

126
00:09:40,830 --> 00:09:44,791
the last time you two were here,
you had a big argument and then left.

127
00:09:44,792 --> 00:09:47,587
I take it things have changed
quite a bit since then?

128
00:09:48,421 --> 00:09:51,382
I haven't regained my memory,
but I guess you could say

129
00:09:52,341 --> 00:09:54,175
I regained my trust in him.

130
00:09:54,176 --> 00:09:55,678
Trust? I see.

131
00:09:57,680 --> 00:10:00,308
Isn't that just how things go
between a man and a woman?

132
00:10:06,314 --> 00:10:09,024
Let's go ahead with the treatment
as planned.

133
00:10:09,025 --> 00:10:11,192
You mentioned physical therapy,
didn't you?

134
00:10:11,193 --> 00:10:12,028
Yes, I did.

135
00:10:12,945 --> 00:10:16,489
It's called TMS, and we use
magnetic pulses on the cerebral cortex,

136
00:10:16,490 --> 00:10:18,116
which stores long-term memory.

137
00:10:18,117 --> 00:10:20,577
If we're lucky,
it will stimulate the area,

138
00:10:20,578 --> 00:10:22,162
and her memory will come back.

139
00:10:22,163 --> 00:10:25,790
Is it painful, by any chance?
Might it cause severe headaches or--

140
00:10:25,791 --> 00:10:28,836
Remember when our teacher whacked you
for picking A's in the multiple choice?

141
00:10:29,503 --> 00:10:31,255
It'll hurt less than that.

142
00:10:36,927 --> 00:10:39,013
So, TMS first, then…

143
00:10:40,348 --> 00:10:41,890
TMS TREATMENT ROOM

144
00:10:41,891 --> 00:10:45,644
You were a mess, saying you were scared
and couldn't believe him and whatnot.

145
00:10:45,645 --> 00:10:49,357
Women sure are hard to read.

146
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:53,277
Well, things happened.

147
00:10:53,861 --> 00:10:55,905
I believe everything Jang Tae-ha says now.

148
00:10:57,073 --> 00:10:59,200
Then why bother with
getting your memory back?

149
00:11:02,328 --> 00:11:04,580
Because I want to remember our past.

150
00:11:05,748 --> 00:11:08,584
I think it's true
that my life was nothing special,

151
00:11:09,585 --> 00:11:13,171
but Jang Tae-ha
seems to have liked me a lot regardless.

152
00:11:13,172 --> 00:11:16,007
Right now, only he remembers that.

153
00:11:16,008 --> 00:11:17,592
How lonely must that be?

154
00:11:17,593 --> 00:11:21,931
Not being able to share the memories
you made with the person you love.

155
00:11:26,727 --> 00:11:29,647
- Was it okay?
- Yeah, I didn't feel a thing.

156
00:11:31,315 --> 00:11:32,232
Here.

157
00:11:32,233 --> 00:11:33,067
Thanks.

158
00:11:33,651 --> 00:11:34,527
Don't mention it.

159
00:11:36,153 --> 00:11:37,196
We'll get going.

160
00:11:38,656 --> 00:11:39,782
Let's go.

161
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:56,256
Ms. Lee Chae-yeon.

162
00:11:56,257 --> 00:11:57,383
Yes.

163
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:05,266
That woman who was your classmate.

164
00:12:05,933 --> 00:12:07,351
I have a bad feeling about her.

165
00:12:07,852 --> 00:12:08,768
Why?

166
00:12:08,769 --> 00:12:13,441
Women can easily sniff out other women
who are interested in their men.

167
00:12:14,024 --> 00:12:17,277
The way she defended you
and had a go at me last time.

168
00:12:17,278 --> 00:12:19,947
And the way she looks at you.

169
00:12:23,242 --> 00:12:24,535
Why are you laughing?

170
00:12:25,369 --> 00:12:27,872
Could it be that she likes you?

171
00:12:28,914 --> 00:12:30,707
- No way.
- What do you mean "no way"?

172
00:12:30,708 --> 00:12:33,419
Didn't you see her earlier?
She was doing all this.

173
00:12:34,003 --> 00:12:36,588
Her hair was already tucked
behind her ear.

174
00:12:36,589 --> 00:12:40,092
There was no hair left to tuck,
but she kept doing this.

175
00:12:40,676 --> 00:12:45,556
That's a subconscious way of flirting
to show off her femininity and neckline.

176
00:12:46,599 --> 00:12:49,018
Let's go to the gym.
Mr. Hong's treating us to shrimp.

177
00:12:58,152 --> 00:13:02,363
- Is the treatment she got today effective?
- Thank you.

178
00:13:02,364 --> 00:13:05,867
They can't guarantee anything.
We can only hope for the best.

179
00:13:05,868 --> 00:13:06,952
Sure.

180
00:13:14,084 --> 00:13:15,419
That shrimp's gonna freeze.

181
00:13:21,759 --> 00:13:23,594
- Eat up.
- Okay.

182
00:13:24,804 --> 00:13:29,224
You're really living up to your reputation
as the village romantic.

183
00:13:29,225 --> 00:13:30,768
As if you're the only lovebirds.

184
00:13:31,769 --> 00:13:32,812
We're lovebirds too.

185
00:13:34,855 --> 00:13:36,440
- Here.
- Open up.

186
00:13:41,153 --> 00:13:43,239
Is this a village of love?

187
00:13:44,782 --> 00:13:47,617
I have shrimp whiskers
stuck under my nails

188
00:13:47,618 --> 00:13:50,996
from peeling and eating shrimp
all by my lonesome self.

189
00:13:52,623 --> 00:13:54,083
Here, eat up.

190
00:13:54,875 --> 00:13:56,001
Thank you.

191
00:13:56,627 --> 00:13:57,545
Thanks.

192
00:13:58,587 --> 00:13:59,463
- Hilarious.
- Thanks.

193
00:14:03,050 --> 00:14:06,554
Please go on and get some sleep.
I'll be back after a quick smoke.

194
00:14:08,013 --> 00:14:08,973
So funny.

195
00:14:09,640 --> 00:14:10,599
Thank you.

196
00:14:11,725 --> 00:14:14,478
Is today the day the car will be ready?

197
00:14:16,689 --> 00:14:19,692
Sorry? Yes, it'll be ready today.

198
00:14:20,276 --> 00:14:23,070
He says he bought a good one
to drive you around in.

199
00:14:26,907 --> 00:14:28,325
Shall we pick it up together?

200
00:14:30,619 --> 00:14:31,828
No, thanks.

201
00:14:31,829 --> 00:14:35,291
You're doing all that for me,
so I want to earn my keep.

202
00:14:36,125 --> 00:14:37,041
Earn your keep?

203
00:14:37,042 --> 00:14:39,169
You said I worked
at your grandma's taffy shop.

204
00:14:39,837 --> 00:14:41,714
I should go back to my old job.

205
00:14:42,214 --> 00:14:44,550
I bet I could learn the ropes
pretty quickly.

206
00:14:46,010 --> 00:14:47,428
It didn't look too difficult.

207
00:14:47,970 --> 00:14:49,930
You want me to do all this?

208
00:14:53,559 --> 00:14:55,435
All you have to do is scoop and pour.

209
00:14:55,436 --> 00:14:57,813
What's so hard about that?

210
00:14:58,564 --> 00:15:00,023
Try it.

211
00:15:00,024 --> 00:15:02,860
Do you have any thick gloves I could …

212
00:15:09,241 --> 00:15:10,950
- Grab it already.
- Yes, ma'am.

213
00:15:10,951 --> 00:15:13,454
Such a neat freak.

214
00:15:15,456 --> 00:15:16,916
It's hot!

215
00:15:18,042 --> 00:15:20,501
- Did you burn yourself?
- No, I'm okay.

216
00:15:20,502 --> 00:15:22,045
What should I do?

217
00:15:22,046 --> 00:15:23,129
Oh no.

218
00:15:23,130 --> 00:15:26,300
I'm sorry. Do you have another one?

219
00:15:28,427 --> 00:15:30,136
Do you have a ladle or something?

220
00:15:30,137 --> 00:15:32,931
The taffy would stick to something
like that.

221
00:15:32,932 --> 00:15:37,019
You need to use a lacquered bowl
so the taffy can slide right off!

222
00:15:37,811 --> 00:15:39,980
So there's a reason for everything.

223
00:15:40,564 --> 00:15:41,481
I'm so sorry.

224
00:15:41,482 --> 00:15:44,693
If your hand's okay,
go outside and ask around for a bowl.

225
00:15:53,452 --> 00:15:55,579
That should be enough to dull them, right?

226
00:16:02,378 --> 00:16:05,506
I'm definitely going to cut myself.

227
00:16:06,006 --> 00:16:07,549
Good grief.

228
00:16:08,676 --> 00:16:12,763
Why did my spiritual powers
have to just up and disappear?

229
00:16:14,056 --> 00:16:16,308
My spiritual powers are gone,

230
00:16:16,892 --> 00:16:20,396
and soon my feet will be gone too.

231
00:16:31,115 --> 00:16:33,659
<i>What is she doing here?
How long has she been there?</i>

232
00:16:34,284 --> 00:16:36,494
<i>Did she hear everything?</i>

233
00:16:36,495 --> 00:16:38,663
I need to borrow a gourd bowl.

234
00:16:38,664 --> 00:16:39,622
What?

235
00:16:39,623 --> 00:16:40,916
A gourd bowl.

236
00:16:41,667 --> 00:16:43,877
Right, a gourd bowl.

237
00:16:46,296 --> 00:16:47,464
Yeah, okay.

238
00:16:48,716 --> 00:16:51,926
GARAK SHAMAN

239
00:16:51,927 --> 00:16:52,761
What the heck?

240
00:16:53,262 --> 00:16:55,389
So she really doesn't have
spiritual powers.

241
00:16:57,141 --> 00:16:59,101
AN MENTAL HEALTH CLINIC

242
00:16:59,685 --> 00:17:00,977
LETTER OF RESIGNATION

243
00:17:00,978 --> 00:17:04,272
I'll work on the handover,
so find my replacement as soon as you can.

244
00:17:04,273 --> 00:17:05,606
You're really doing this?

245
00:17:05,607 --> 00:17:07,650
How can we work together
after breaking up?

246
00:17:07,651 --> 00:17:09,611
- Hey, Min Su-ji.
- Yeah, what?

247
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:17,995
Do you even have somewhere to go
if you quit?

248
00:17:21,498 --> 00:17:22,833
I'll figure something out.

249
00:17:32,301 --> 00:17:35,345
That's not what I meant.
Why do I keep saying things like that?

250
00:17:36,263 --> 00:17:37,598
Damn it.

251
00:17:42,019 --> 00:17:45,563
What? Well, look who it is! It's Su-ji!

252
00:17:45,564 --> 00:17:47,565
- Have you been well?
- Of course!

253
00:17:47,566 --> 00:17:49,651
What brings you to Taffy Village?

254
00:17:50,319 --> 00:17:51,903
I just thought I'd stop by.

255
00:17:51,904 --> 00:17:54,155
Can I get a kimchi stew
and a bottle of soju?

256
00:17:54,156 --> 00:17:55,491
Of course.

257
00:17:58,243 --> 00:18:02,705
Feels like yesterday you were in uniform.
Now you're old enough to drink?

258
00:18:02,706 --> 00:18:03,915
Oh, aren't you pretty!

259
00:18:03,916 --> 00:18:06,209
Su-ji, you're old enough
to get married now.

260
00:18:06,210 --> 00:18:10,088
What's with the marriage talk
from the get-go?

261
00:18:10,089 --> 00:18:12,007
Are you happy because you're married?

262
00:18:13,759 --> 00:18:18,221
Didn't you say that night at the motel
near Gujin rotary with Pil-seung's father

263
00:18:18,222 --> 00:18:20,348
was the biggest mistake of your life?

264
00:18:20,349 --> 00:18:22,475
Su-ji, don't you ever get married.

265
00:18:22,476 --> 00:18:24,310
But still,

266
00:18:24,311 --> 00:18:27,313
if everyone's married,
and you're the only one left,

267
00:18:27,314 --> 00:18:28,898
it would get lonely.

268
00:18:28,899 --> 00:18:29,982
I guess you're right.

269
00:18:29,983 --> 00:18:33,111
Come to think of it,
aren't you the same age as Tae-ha?

270
00:18:33,112 --> 00:18:34,862
- That's right.
- Yeah.

271
00:18:34,863 --> 00:18:37,574
Tae-ha brought home a wife he adores
and started a family.

272
00:18:38,659 --> 00:18:41,078
- Su-ji, don't you have anyone?
- Don't you?

273
00:18:42,538 --> 00:18:44,373
No, I don't.

274
00:18:49,419 --> 00:18:51,630
Have a drink. Go on.

275
00:19:16,738 --> 00:19:19,073
WALNUTS
BOOSTS BRAIN HEALTH AND MEMORY

276
00:19:19,074 --> 00:19:20,324
Thank you.

277
00:19:20,325 --> 00:19:21,784
Su-ji, will you be okay?

278
00:19:21,785 --> 00:19:24,912
- I'm totally fine. I swear.
- Goodness, I'm worried.

279
00:19:24,913 --> 00:19:26,581
- I'll get going.
- Careful now.

280
00:19:26,582 --> 00:19:28,000
Will you be okay?

281
00:19:31,086 --> 00:19:32,838
Jang Tae-ha.

282
00:19:41,638 --> 00:19:42,555
You're…

283
00:19:42,556 --> 00:19:45,892
Su-ji. Min Su-ji.

284
00:19:45,893 --> 00:19:47,769
Don't you dare call me Sun-deok again.

285
00:19:48,562 --> 00:19:49,396
Right.

286
00:19:51,690 --> 00:19:52,607
Are you okay?

287
00:19:52,608 --> 00:19:54,359
If I'm not okay,

288
00:19:55,360 --> 00:19:56,570
will you take me home?

289
00:19:59,031 --> 00:19:59,865
Look at that.

290
00:20:01,617 --> 00:20:03,785
I have to get home.

291
00:20:05,078 --> 00:20:06,163
Right, Gi-jun.

292
00:20:06,914 --> 00:20:09,166
You work with Gi-jun, don't you? Hold on.

293
00:20:12,377 --> 00:20:13,670
She grabbed his hand!

294
00:20:14,504 --> 00:20:15,880
Don't.

295
00:20:15,881 --> 00:20:16,797
What?

296
00:20:16,798 --> 00:20:19,426
I'm saying don't call him.

297
00:20:26,642 --> 00:20:28,435
If I were your girlfriend,

298
00:20:29,811 --> 00:20:32,064
could I have been loved too?

299
00:20:35,025 --> 00:20:35,943
Stop right there.

300
00:20:37,945 --> 00:20:39,780
- What is it?
- Eun-sae's here.

301
00:20:40,280 --> 00:20:41,657
Go Eun-sae.

302
00:20:50,123 --> 00:20:51,792
No need to be flustered.

303
00:20:52,292 --> 00:20:53,794
Just do as I say from now on.

304
00:20:57,506 --> 00:20:58,757
Arms by your sides.

305
00:21:06,807 --> 00:21:08,100
Three steps back.

306
00:21:19,569 --> 00:21:21,029
You're dead meat.

307
00:21:30,163 --> 00:21:31,164
Excuse me.

308
00:21:32,833 --> 00:21:34,126
Your fly's open.

309
00:21:38,130 --> 00:21:42,217
I won't assume you're 100% faking
being drunk.

310
00:21:42,801 --> 00:21:46,972
But if you had enough sense
to zip up your damn fly,

311
00:21:48,432 --> 00:21:51,226
you shouldn't be grabbing
a taken man's hand.

312
00:22:00,402 --> 00:22:01,862
Your address.

313
00:22:03,030 --> 00:22:04,697
Jangmi Mansion.

314
00:22:04,698 --> 00:22:06,116
Jangmi Mansion?

315
00:22:06,616 --> 00:22:08,243
Okay.

316
00:22:10,120 --> 00:22:11,662
Hi, Gang-rok.

317
00:22:11,663 --> 00:22:14,582
You told me to think of you
as a little brother at my disposal,

318
00:22:14,583 --> 00:22:15,917
so do me a favor.

319
00:22:17,419 --> 00:22:19,713
There's a drunk lady over here.

320
00:22:20,297 --> 00:22:22,382
Please escort her home.

321
00:22:26,678 --> 00:22:27,512
How impressive.

322
00:22:49,910 --> 00:22:51,912
<i>Impact detected.</i>

323
00:22:55,374 --> 00:22:57,167
The car's nice, isn't it?

324
00:22:58,543 --> 00:23:01,712
The plastic wrap is still on.
Shall we tear it off together later?

325
00:23:01,713 --> 00:23:03,214
Forget the plastic wrap.

326
00:23:03,215 --> 00:23:06,468
I wanted to tear out that girl's hair
but held myself back,

327
00:23:07,052 --> 00:23:08,470
so let's just go quietly.

328
00:23:25,320 --> 00:23:29,116
You know, I only held her up.

329
00:23:31,993 --> 00:23:33,370
So she wouldn't fall.

330
00:23:33,870 --> 00:23:36,122
If you face-plant on asphalt,

331
00:23:36,123 --> 00:23:38,749
you're in big trouble.
You could shatter your cheekbones.

332
00:23:38,750 --> 00:23:42,169
Why are that woman's cheekbones
any of your concern?

333
00:23:42,170 --> 00:23:43,004
Huh?

334
00:23:43,505 --> 00:23:45,840
It's as if you want to save
the entire world.

335
00:23:45,841 --> 00:23:48,093
Is it your dream to be an Avenger?

336
00:23:48,885 --> 00:23:50,928
Don't you know how to draw lines?

337
00:23:50,929 --> 00:23:53,890
You shouldn't have left her an opening.
You let her touch…

338
00:23:55,642 --> 00:23:58,645
Why would you let her touch you?

339
00:23:59,146 --> 00:24:02,274
Only I'm allowed to do that. Only me.

340
00:24:05,152 --> 00:24:05,986
You're smiling?

341
00:24:06,945 --> 00:24:08,029
Is this funny to you?

342
00:24:08,530 --> 00:24:12,408
Do you think
I'm being jealous or something?

343
00:24:12,409 --> 00:24:14,743
I'm talking about basic common sense here.

344
00:24:14,744 --> 00:24:16,913
Okay, it was wrong of me.

345
00:24:22,419 --> 00:24:23,670
I'm sorry.

346
00:24:26,506 --> 00:24:28,383
I'm serious.

347
00:24:28,967 --> 00:24:32,679
See what'll happen
if you ever touch another woman again.

348
00:24:34,264 --> 00:24:35,515
What's that?

349
00:24:36,099 --> 00:24:37,975
Some walnuts.

350
00:24:37,976 --> 00:24:40,436
They look like brains,
so they're brain food.

351
00:24:40,437 --> 00:24:42,189
To help you regain your memory.

352
00:24:43,648 --> 00:24:46,484
Come on, that's ridiculous.

353
00:24:46,485 --> 00:24:49,278
So, what, you drink milk
if you want fair skin

354
00:24:49,279 --> 00:24:52,032
and eat gochujang if you want red lips?

355
00:24:58,079 --> 00:24:59,247
What's wrong?

356
00:25:04,252 --> 00:25:05,462
Are you okay?

357
00:25:07,839 --> 00:25:09,216
I think

358
00:25:10,550 --> 00:25:11,885
I remember something.

359
00:25:16,848 --> 00:25:18,433
Go Ji-won!

360
00:25:19,184 --> 00:25:22,394
I said I'll make you eat gochujang
if you leave food, didn't I?

361
00:25:22,395 --> 00:25:23,480
Eat it!

362
00:25:24,105 --> 00:25:26,357
Eat! I said eat!

363
00:25:26,358 --> 00:25:27,275
Open!

364
00:25:27,859 --> 00:25:30,487
Open your mouth! Wide! Open!

365
00:25:49,256 --> 00:25:50,465
Thank you.

366
00:25:55,136 --> 00:25:55,971
Feel better?

367
00:25:57,055 --> 00:25:58,056
Yeah.

368
00:25:58,723 --> 00:26:01,393
I guess the treatment I got today worked.

369
00:26:02,227 --> 00:26:04,062
You remembered being at the orphanage?

370
00:26:05,188 --> 00:26:06,106
Yes.

371
00:26:07,274 --> 00:26:09,109
Not all of it,

372
00:26:09,985 --> 00:26:12,320
but bits and pieces, here and there.

373
00:26:15,156 --> 00:26:16,991
After I woke up with my memory gone,

374
00:26:16,992 --> 00:26:20,495
I really didn't want to go
to a government facility for some reason.

375
00:26:22,080 --> 00:26:23,623
Now I know why.

376
00:26:24,207 --> 00:26:25,958
<i>I guess my body remembered.</i>

377
00:26:25,959 --> 00:26:29,754
I told you to smile big
when they come to take pictures.

378
00:26:30,338 --> 00:26:33,757
<i>At the orphanage,
we got group punishments all the time.</i>

379
00:26:33,758 --> 00:26:34,758
Go Ji-won!

380
00:26:34,759 --> 00:26:37,928
<i>In the middle of winter,
we were often kicked out barefoot.</i>

381
00:26:37,929 --> 00:26:38,930
Outside.

382
00:26:40,807 --> 00:26:44,436
<i>Just thinking about
how the cold crept into my feet…</i>

383
00:26:45,895 --> 00:26:47,397
<i>It still gives me the chills.</i>

384
00:26:49,899 --> 00:26:52,193
<i>They abused you?</i>

385
00:26:53,612 --> 00:26:57,449
<i>Being kids without guardians
made us easy targets.</i>

386
00:27:06,708 --> 00:27:10,086
And another thing.
We were dragged off to work.

387
00:27:11,546 --> 00:27:12,504
What?

388
00:27:12,505 --> 00:27:16,300
On weekends, we went to a rural area
about three hours away

389
00:27:16,301 --> 00:27:17,218
to work on a farm.

390
00:27:17,802 --> 00:27:21,221
<i>I remember the trip to the country
being really rough.</i>

391
00:27:21,222 --> 00:27:23,807
<i>We were all crammed in a van</i>

392
00:27:23,808 --> 00:27:24,934
for three hours.

393
00:27:25,435 --> 00:27:28,937
"Oh, I wish I could find
a discarded MP3 player or something."

394
00:27:28,938 --> 00:27:33,026
"Then I could listen to my favorite
god songs to help me get through it."

395
00:27:33,860 --> 00:27:36,237
I think I had innocent thoughts like that.

396
00:27:37,447 --> 00:27:40,158
Those things were a luxury
for kids like me.

397
00:27:47,123 --> 00:27:48,375
And

398
00:27:49,125 --> 00:27:52,795
there were also thugs
who took the orphanage's funds.

399
00:27:52,796 --> 00:27:55,130
<i>When they got angry,</i>

400
00:27:55,131 --> 00:27:59,803
<i>they would beat up
the middle school boys at the orphanage.</i>

401
00:28:00,303 --> 00:28:02,222
<i>I was terrified.</i>

402
00:28:03,973 --> 00:28:08,436
I guess that's why
I hate violence so much.

403
00:28:16,236 --> 00:28:18,071
What do you hate, Tae-ha?

404
00:28:20,865 --> 00:28:21,782
What?

405
00:28:21,783 --> 00:28:25,494
I don't have any memories,
so I don't know much about you.

406
00:28:25,495 --> 00:28:27,830
Tell me everything again, one by one.

407
00:28:27,831 --> 00:28:30,958
First off, your favorite things are
boxing and gochujang stew.

408
00:28:30,959 --> 00:28:33,086
Next, what don't you like?

409
00:28:38,091 --> 00:28:38,925
Rain.

410
00:28:39,676 --> 00:28:40,510
Rain?

411
00:28:42,303 --> 00:28:44,222
On the hardest days of my life,

412
00:28:44,723 --> 00:28:46,558
it always rained, for some reason.

413
00:28:52,355 --> 00:28:54,607
BODEUM HOSPITAL CANCER CENTER

414
00:29:02,657 --> 00:29:04,576
<i>Like the day Grandma collapsed…</i>

415
00:29:08,580 --> 00:29:10,498
<i>and the day I quit boxing.</i>

416
00:29:11,124 --> 00:29:14,210
<i>Just… days like those.</i>

417
00:29:18,590 --> 00:29:22,719
TAEREUNG NATIONAL TRAINING CENTER

418
00:29:25,722 --> 00:29:27,474
<i>In my bleakest moments,</i>

419
00:29:28,183 --> 00:29:29,142
<i>there was nothing</i>

420
00:29:29,934 --> 00:29:32,061
<i>to shield me from the rain.</i>

421
00:29:33,271 --> 00:29:34,105
It felt like

422
00:29:35,231 --> 00:29:37,484
a reminder of just how hopeless
things were.

423
00:29:39,652 --> 00:29:40,820
So I don't like rain.

424
00:29:46,451 --> 00:29:48,661
I heard your story from Mr. Hong.

425
00:29:50,747 --> 00:29:53,666
Don't you regret
the decision you made back then?

426
00:29:54,834 --> 00:29:55,835
I don't.

427
00:29:56,628 --> 00:29:58,755
Because I protected
what I wanted to protect.

428
00:30:05,470 --> 00:30:06,387
Thank you.

429
00:30:08,932 --> 00:30:10,266
For protecting me too.

430
00:30:11,976 --> 00:30:13,853
If it had been anyone else,

431
00:30:15,563 --> 00:30:19,526
I think they would've given up on me
when I lost my memory and my mind.

432
00:30:25,824 --> 00:30:29,369
Now that I have some of my memories back,
I'm even more grateful to you.

433
00:30:31,746 --> 00:30:32,956
I'm glad

434
00:30:33,998 --> 00:30:35,959
that you're my boyfriend.

435
00:31:13,496 --> 00:31:14,455
I'm back!

436
00:31:15,373 --> 00:31:17,082
Right, yeah.

437
00:31:17,083 --> 00:31:18,126
Hello.

438
00:31:18,710 --> 00:31:21,129
- You're… here.
- Why do you have the lights off?

439
00:31:21,754 --> 00:31:23,339
I took the drunk lady home.

440
00:31:23,923 --> 00:31:27,218
I even rode the taxi with her
and saw her get inside safely.

441
00:31:28,720 --> 00:31:32,389
And on my way back, I saw someone
selling flower-shaped buns.

442
00:31:32,390 --> 00:31:33,224
Here.

443
00:31:34,851 --> 00:31:36,144
Would you like some?

444
00:31:39,898 --> 00:31:42,566
Buns at this hour?

445
00:31:42,567 --> 00:31:45,361
I ought to kick you in the buns.

446
00:31:45,862 --> 00:31:49,490
Yeah, eating them will only make you fat.
You're starting to get a belly.

447
00:31:52,994 --> 00:31:55,622
HONG'S BOXING GYM

448
00:31:58,333 --> 00:32:02,002
I got some nice sea bream at the market
and cooked it for you all.

449
00:32:02,003 --> 00:32:04,588
- I forgot water.
- I'll get it.

450
00:32:04,589 --> 00:32:05,506
No, please.

451
00:32:11,095 --> 00:32:12,388
It's just that…

452
00:32:13,848 --> 00:32:15,766
Why would you let her touch you?

453
00:32:15,767 --> 00:32:18,353
Only I'm allowed to do that. Only me.

454
00:32:18,978 --> 00:32:22,106
I was told not to make
any physical contact with other women.

455
00:32:23,942 --> 00:32:24,859
What a load of crap.

456
00:32:25,860 --> 00:32:27,278
Are you out of your mind?

457
00:32:27,904 --> 00:32:30,865
Just leave him be.
He sure learned that well.

458
00:32:33,576 --> 00:32:34,410
Give that here.

459
00:32:36,079 --> 00:32:38,538
Eun-sae, will you be going
to the taffy shop today?

460
00:32:38,539 --> 00:32:40,041
The shop is closed today.

461
00:32:40,875 --> 00:32:42,460
Then shall we go to see the ritual?

462
00:32:43,086 --> 00:32:44,461
- The ritual?
- Yeah.

463
00:32:44,462 --> 00:32:46,589
Maeng-suk is performing
a shamanic ritual today.

464
00:32:47,090 --> 00:32:49,008
I see.

465
00:32:51,552 --> 00:32:52,929
Wait, I'm sorry.

466
00:32:53,429 --> 00:32:55,515
I forgot that I had something to do today.

467
00:32:56,224 --> 00:32:58,893
I was the one who suggested it,
but I'm flaking.

468
00:32:59,394 --> 00:33:02,104
I'll be back after a quick call.
Please go ahead.

469
00:33:02,105 --> 00:33:05,857
Why is he moving around so much
with that injured foot of his?

470
00:33:05,858 --> 00:33:07,276
Just leave him be.

471
00:33:08,987 --> 00:33:12,030
Wow, this soup is really something.

472
00:33:12,031 --> 00:33:12,991
Is it?

473
00:33:14,701 --> 00:33:15,910
That was delicious.

474
00:33:17,537 --> 00:33:18,705
You're leaving already?

475
00:33:20,206 --> 00:33:21,416
We finished eating.

476
00:33:22,166 --> 00:33:23,001
I'll get going.

477
00:33:23,584 --> 00:33:26,963
Okay. Remember to take your meds
and call if anything happens.

478
00:33:29,507 --> 00:33:31,217
See you later.

479
00:33:37,348 --> 00:33:39,100
Are you that happy?

480
00:33:44,230 --> 00:33:45,856
Why are you doing this?

481
00:33:45,857 --> 00:33:47,357
- Follow me quietly.
- Sorry?

482
00:33:47,358 --> 00:33:48,693
But, sir!

483
00:33:49,736 --> 00:33:51,028
My leg…

484
00:33:51,029 --> 00:33:53,114
Seriously, why are you doing this?

485
00:33:58,828 --> 00:34:02,623
Tell me. What are you up to?
Did Baek Sang-gil send you?

486
00:34:03,374 --> 00:34:06,460
No. Why would he send me?
I didn't even see his face when I left--

487
00:34:06,461 --> 00:34:07,795
Keep it down, damn it.

488
00:34:14,761 --> 00:34:16,929
Then who are you reporting to,
and about what?

489
00:34:17,555 --> 00:34:18,889
Where do you go at dawn?

490
00:34:18,890 --> 00:34:21,768
And why do you have two phones?
Explain it all. In detail.

491
00:34:31,652 --> 00:34:32,653
I…

492
00:34:37,325 --> 00:34:39,077
do YouTube live streams.

493
00:34:41,079 --> 00:34:43,915
- What?
- I review overseas soccer games.

494
00:34:44,499 --> 00:34:45,500
The phones.

495
00:34:47,376 --> 00:34:51,172
I have two because I watch soccer on one
while I film myself with the other.

496
00:34:51,756 --> 00:34:55,675
I've been leaving at dawn to stream
because that's when overseas games happen.

497
00:34:55,676 --> 00:34:58,345
I couldn't do it at home,
where you guys were sleeping.

498
00:34:58,346 --> 00:35:01,432
And he goes for it!
Up the field. On the other side!

499
00:35:02,308 --> 00:35:04,142
Oh, Ashley!

500
00:35:04,143 --> 00:35:06,104
This one's for you guys!

501
00:35:06,604 --> 00:35:07,730
Thank you!

502
00:35:09,357 --> 00:35:11,192
Guys, thank…

503
00:35:15,113 --> 00:35:16,613
I cover my face,

504
00:35:16,614 --> 00:35:20,534
and I avoid places that might give away
where we are, so you don't have to worry.

505
00:35:20,535 --> 00:35:23,245
And the calls are with my YouTube agency.

506
00:35:23,246 --> 00:35:25,038
They ask me when I can stream.

507
00:35:25,039 --> 00:35:27,333
The calls were me sharing my schedule.

508
00:35:28,668 --> 00:35:31,170
I quit the gang,
but I still needed to make a living.

509
00:35:31,921 --> 00:35:34,714
And my foot was like this.

510
00:35:34,715 --> 00:35:36,342
There was nothing I could do.

511
00:35:36,843 --> 00:35:40,263
So I asked myself,
"What was it that I truly liked?"

512
00:35:42,265 --> 00:35:44,392
"What did I want to become?"

513
00:35:46,394 --> 00:35:48,729
That's how I started doing this.

514
00:35:51,858 --> 00:35:54,402
If you don't believe me,
check for yourself.

515
00:36:11,169 --> 00:36:14,380
<i>Hello, this is Studio Yes,
a YouTube content agency.</i>

516
00:36:32,982 --> 00:36:34,233
Why is this so scuffed?

517
00:36:40,489 --> 00:36:41,908
When does the cast come off?

518
00:36:48,748 --> 00:36:52,042
I understand why you're so worried.

519
00:36:52,043 --> 00:36:55,587
Because if Chairman Baek…
I mean, if Baek Sang-gil finds out,

520
00:36:55,588 --> 00:36:58,549
neither you nor the prosecutor
will survive.

521
00:37:01,260 --> 00:37:03,261
The stowaway boat plan is getting close.

522
00:37:03,262 --> 00:37:04,805
Is the prosecutor getting better?

523
00:37:07,141 --> 00:37:09,018
Yesterday, she remembered her childhood.

524
00:37:09,644 --> 00:37:11,520
She'll likely regain her memory soon.

525
00:37:13,022 --> 00:37:14,690
I really hope that happens.

526
00:37:15,691 --> 00:37:19,862
If it does, it will be easier
to persuade her to leave the country,

527
00:37:20,947 --> 00:37:23,699
but wouldn't she also find out
that you're not her boyfriend?

528
00:37:25,368 --> 00:37:28,037
That would mean losing
the relationship you have now.

529
00:37:29,330 --> 00:37:31,249
Will you be okay with that?

530
00:37:35,544 --> 00:37:39,131
It doesn't matter what happens to me
as long as Go Eun-sae lives.

531
00:38:20,548 --> 00:38:22,591
- She's getting on the blades.
- She is!

532
00:38:23,175 --> 00:38:24,593
It's so fascinating.

533
00:38:42,862 --> 00:38:44,738
What's taking her so long?

534
00:38:44,739 --> 00:38:46,823
- What's going on?
- She's not getting on.

535
00:38:46,824 --> 00:38:50,202
- Why isn't she getting on them?
- What's she doing?

536
00:38:55,041 --> 00:38:56,751
Hurry up already!

537
00:39:03,841 --> 00:39:06,051
Snake! It's a snake!

538
00:39:06,052 --> 00:39:07,344
- Snake?
- A snake?

539
00:39:07,345 --> 00:39:09,263
A snake! There's a snake!

540
00:39:10,681 --> 00:39:11,806
What the heck?

541
00:39:11,807 --> 00:39:15,894
Isn't it bad luck to see snakes
or animal carcasses during a ritual?

542
00:39:15,895 --> 00:39:19,022
Yeah, they say you shouldn't perform
a shamanic ritual if you see a snake.

543
00:39:19,023 --> 00:39:20,399
They say it won't work.

544
00:39:20,900 --> 00:39:22,734
It's no good if it won't work!

545
00:39:22,735 --> 00:39:25,696
Then I guess we should call it a day.

546
00:39:27,823 --> 00:39:29,909
Hey, lady! Come down!

547
00:39:34,538 --> 00:39:35,456
Okay.

548
00:39:38,334 --> 00:39:39,418
Let's stop.

549
00:39:40,419 --> 00:39:42,253
Where did the snake even come from?

550
00:39:42,254 --> 00:39:43,506
Let's stop.

551
00:39:47,259 --> 00:39:48,928
I'm going to stop now!

552
00:39:49,762 --> 00:39:52,764
- She's stopping the ritual?
- She's stopping?

553
00:39:52,765 --> 00:39:54,016
Yes!

554
00:39:54,850 --> 00:39:56,893
I'm going to stop!

555
00:39:56,894 --> 00:39:57,852
What's wrong?

556
00:39:57,853 --> 00:39:59,188
What's going on?

557
00:40:01,482 --> 00:40:03,401
- What's going on?
- What's happening?

558
00:40:08,739 --> 00:40:10,074
What…

559
00:40:30,302 --> 00:40:31,470
I tried everything…

560
00:40:34,223 --> 00:40:36,642
but once the spirit leaves,
it doesn't come back.

561
00:40:40,229 --> 00:40:42,564
I'd been thinking about quitting
for a while,

562
00:40:42,565 --> 00:40:44,607
but I couldn't bring myself to do it.

563
00:40:44,608 --> 00:40:48,069
After losing my husband and child,
I only had my fortune-telling business.

564
00:40:48,070 --> 00:40:49,821
If I lost that too,

565
00:40:49,822 --> 00:40:52,323
my life would be too empty.

566
00:40:52,324 --> 00:40:54,618
What, are we just for show?

567
00:40:55,161 --> 00:40:58,205
You have us, two plump women,
under each of your arms.

568
00:40:58,789 --> 00:41:02,126
Why would your life be empty?

569
00:41:03,752 --> 00:41:06,337
That's why you should have
at least told us.

570
00:41:06,338 --> 00:41:10,801
This must have been gnawing at you
all this time…

571
00:41:13,012 --> 00:41:14,220
You guys are right.

572
00:41:14,221 --> 00:41:19,185
I'd briefly forgotten I had two ladies
who loomed large in my life.

573
00:41:24,231 --> 00:41:28,736
I feel so relieved, like I finally got
a whole load of old poop out of my system.

574
00:41:35,493 --> 00:41:36,660
As for you.

575
00:41:37,912 --> 00:41:39,330
Why did you help me?

576
00:41:44,168 --> 00:41:45,961
Well, I had no other choice.

577
00:41:46,712 --> 00:41:50,633
If I had left you alone,
your feet would've been covered in blood.

578
00:41:53,260 --> 00:41:56,555
I guess you're not a total lost cause.

579
00:41:59,099 --> 00:42:03,395
Well, I realized something
after losing my memory.

580
00:42:04,396 --> 00:42:07,357
I had something,
but it disappeared overnight.

581
00:42:07,358 --> 00:42:09,651
I was flustered

582
00:42:09,652 --> 00:42:11,654
and bitter.

583
00:42:12,238 --> 00:42:14,240
It all felt unfair.

584
00:42:15,407 --> 00:42:17,868
But what I lost wouldn't come back.

585
00:42:18,786 --> 00:42:21,704
My emotions were all over the place
dozens of times a day.

586
00:42:21,705 --> 00:42:24,041
It drove me to the brink of insanity.

587
00:42:25,543 --> 00:42:30,506
Then it occurred to me
that you must have felt the same way.

588
00:42:32,675 --> 00:42:34,051
You two were in the same boat?

589
00:42:35,052 --> 00:42:36,011
I guess.

590
00:42:36,679 --> 00:42:38,388
Life is funny, isn't it?

591
00:42:38,389 --> 00:42:41,141
Just the other day
you were fighting over a broken statue.

592
00:42:42,601 --> 00:42:46,814
Who'd have thought that you two
would now be seeing eye to eye?

593
00:42:47,356 --> 00:42:48,649
Tell me about it.

594
00:42:49,149 --> 00:42:51,609
Let's have a drink,
since we see eye to eye.

595
00:42:51,610 --> 00:42:52,528
Cheers!

596
00:42:53,529 --> 00:42:54,947
Let us join in.

597
00:42:56,323 --> 00:42:57,240
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

598
00:42:57,241 --> 00:42:58,866
<i>Oh, great spirit!</i>

599
00:42:58,867 --> 00:43:04,706
<i>Never come looking for me again</i>

600
00:43:04,707 --> 00:43:08,084
<i>Don't you dare curse me</i>

601
00:43:08,085 --> 00:43:11,714
<i>For being a cruel woman…</i>

602
00:43:12,339 --> 00:43:16,801
<i>I love you to death</i>

603
00:43:16,802 --> 00:43:20,555
<i>Why don't you believe me?</i>

604
00:43:20,556 --> 00:43:23,349
<i>Until the day I die</i>

605
00:43:23,350 --> 00:43:26,686
<i>You're the only one for me</i>

606
00:43:26,687 --> 00:43:31,441
<i>Actually, no, even if I die</i>

607
00:43:31,442 --> 00:43:34,694
<i>You'd still be the only one for me</i>

608
00:43:34,695 --> 00:43:38,281
<i>So please open your heart, believe me</i>

609
00:43:38,282 --> 00:43:39,991
<i>And love me</i>

610
00:43:39,992 --> 00:43:42,452
I love you, ladies!

611
00:43:42,453 --> 00:43:43,662
Careful.

612
00:43:44,204 --> 00:43:48,541
<i>You sexy man, you're my man</i>

613
00:43:48,542 --> 00:43:52,629
<i>You handsome man, you're my man</i>

614
00:43:52,630 --> 00:43:55,673
<i>When this world ends
I'll lose myself in a fantasy</i>

615
00:43:55,674 --> 00:43:57,967
Why did you make her drink so much?

616
00:43:57,968 --> 00:43:59,553
- What?
- Hey!

617
00:44:00,137 --> 00:44:03,890
No, we didn't make her drink.

618
00:44:03,891 --> 00:44:06,518
Your wifey did it all by herself.

619
00:44:09,021 --> 00:44:10,439
It was yummy.

620
00:44:11,065 --> 00:44:13,900
Your wifey is approved! Approved by us!

621
00:44:13,901 --> 00:44:14,984
Approved!

622
00:44:14,985 --> 00:44:16,736
Ladies, let's go for a third round!

623
00:44:16,737 --> 00:44:18,196
- Let's go.
- Sounds good!

624
00:44:18,197 --> 00:44:21,699
Then should we go to the club in town
with the roof that opens?

625
00:44:21,700 --> 00:44:22,784
Let's go!

626
00:44:22,785 --> 00:44:25,203
What are you talking about?
Please get home safely.

627
00:44:25,204 --> 00:44:26,454
Let's go!

628
00:44:26,455 --> 00:44:29,040
<i>My sexy man</i>

629
00:44:29,041 --> 00:44:30,751
- Let's get you home.
- I want to go!

630
00:44:31,752 --> 00:44:34,463
- I can drink more.
- No, you'll die if you drink more.

631
00:44:45,099 --> 00:44:47,101
Hey, it's my boyfriend,

632
00:44:47,810 --> 00:44:49,144
Jang Tae-ha.

633
00:44:50,562 --> 00:44:51,438
Go to sleep.

634
00:44:53,190 --> 00:44:54,399
Okay.

635
00:44:54,400 --> 00:44:58,112
But don't go anywhere

636
00:44:59,029 --> 00:45:00,447
until I fall asleep.

637
00:45:02,533 --> 00:45:03,367
Okay.

638
00:45:46,869 --> 00:45:48,828
<i>If she remembers everything,</i>

639
00:45:48,829 --> 00:45:51,832
<i>that would mean losing
the relationship you have now.</i>

640
00:45:52,624 --> 00:45:54,543
<i>Will you be okay with that?</i>

641
00:46:20,110 --> 00:46:22,988
I'm told that multiple guys
have seen Prosecutor Go.

642
00:46:23,864 --> 00:46:24,989
They saw Go Ji-won?

643
00:46:24,990 --> 00:46:27,408
<i>At first, I also thought
it was impossible, but…</i>

644
00:46:27,409 --> 00:46:29,786
- Hey.
- What is it?

645
00:46:29,787 --> 00:46:31,121
Isn't that Prosecutor Go?

646
00:46:32,915 --> 00:46:35,833
<i>Even though they saw her
at different locations,</i>

647
00:46:35,834 --> 00:46:38,462
<i>their descriptions of her outfit
were identical.</i>

648
00:46:43,175 --> 00:46:45,719
Given the circumstances,
I thought I should tell you first.

649
00:46:58,482 --> 00:47:00,234
If it really is Go Ji-won,

650
00:47:00,734 --> 00:47:02,528
does that mean Jang Tae-ha lost her?

651
00:47:07,199 --> 00:47:08,075
That,

652
00:47:08,992 --> 00:47:10,702
or he let her live.

653
00:47:14,790 --> 00:47:15,999
Impossible.

654
00:47:17,209 --> 00:47:20,545
Sir, what's more worrying
is what Gwak Chi-hyeon said.

655
00:47:20,546 --> 00:47:24,216
Prosecutor Go said she had prepared
one more thing besides the watch.

656
00:47:24,800 --> 00:47:27,010
If Prosecutor Go really is alive,

657
00:47:27,553 --> 00:47:29,304
it's suspicious that she's been quiet.

658
00:47:30,514 --> 00:47:34,101
She could be preparing something
with what Gwak Chi-hyeon mentioned.

659
00:47:49,491 --> 00:47:51,159
My stomach's killing me.

660
00:47:51,869 --> 00:47:53,704
How much did I drink last night?

661
00:47:58,250 --> 00:48:00,668
This is my boyfriend.

662
00:48:00,669 --> 00:48:03,254
He studied international relations
at Hanguk University

663
00:48:03,255 --> 00:48:04,964
and is now the Gangju mayor's aide.

664
00:48:04,965 --> 00:48:06,675
Nice to meet you. I'm Gwak Chi-hyeon.

665
00:48:09,136 --> 00:48:11,346
What… is this?

666
00:48:12,014 --> 00:48:13,473
What is this memory?

667
00:48:14,558 --> 00:48:16,267
<i>He's my boyfriend?</i>

668
00:48:16,268 --> 00:48:17,894
Is he an ex-boyfriend?

669
00:48:17,895 --> 00:48:22,023
I've heard a lot about you from the mayor.
I look forward to your support.

670
00:48:22,024 --> 00:48:23,316
<i>No, it's recent.</i>

671
00:48:23,317 --> 00:48:26,320
- Did you say we dated for two years?
- Yeah.

672
00:48:27,446 --> 00:48:28,906
What is this?

673
00:48:34,536 --> 00:48:35,871
Did you get some sleep?

674
00:48:36,997 --> 00:48:38,206
Is your stomach okay?

675
00:48:40,042 --> 00:48:40,959
Yes.

676
00:48:46,256 --> 00:48:48,759
By any chance,

677
00:48:49,259 --> 00:48:50,594
did I…

678
00:48:51,345 --> 00:48:52,346
Yes?

679
00:48:57,517 --> 00:48:58,518
Never mind.

680
00:49:03,398 --> 00:49:05,400
- You remembered that?
- Yes.

681
00:49:05,901 --> 00:49:07,443
But it doesn't make sense.

682
00:49:07,444 --> 00:49:09,695
I've been dating Jang Tae-ha
for two years.

683
00:49:09,696 --> 00:49:13,450
Why would I introduce someone
named Gwak Chi-hyeon as my boyfriend?

684
00:49:13,951 --> 00:49:15,284
So I was wondering,

685
00:49:15,285 --> 00:49:18,288
could this be a memory of a dream
or something I imagined?

686
00:49:20,374 --> 00:49:23,000
I'm not sure.
It's not completely impossible.

687
00:49:23,001 --> 00:49:25,128
But there's no way to be sure.

688
00:49:26,755 --> 00:49:27,798
Wait a minute.

689
00:49:29,341 --> 00:49:30,842
Actually, there might be a way.

690
00:49:32,469 --> 00:49:35,680
- How?
- Didn't you say he studied at Hanguk Uni?

691
00:49:35,681 --> 00:49:39,016
- Yes.
- I went to med school there!

692
00:49:39,017 --> 00:49:40,017
Look behind you.

693
00:49:40,018 --> 00:49:41,269
Hold on, one second.

694
00:49:41,770 --> 00:49:44,271
Let me check with a friend
who was in that department.

695
00:49:44,272 --> 00:49:45,523
DIRECTOR AN GI-JUN

696
00:49:45,524 --> 00:49:47,985
HANGUK UNIVERSITY SCHOOL OF MEDICINE

697
00:49:58,036 --> 00:50:00,330
CHAIRMAN BAEK SANG-GIL

698
00:50:06,628 --> 00:50:07,545
How did it go?

699
00:50:07,546 --> 00:50:11,382
They're yet to find CCTV footage
of the person they think is Prosecutor Go.

700
00:50:11,383 --> 00:50:14,803
If that bitch really is alive,
we don't have time to waste like this.

701
00:50:15,470 --> 00:50:17,180
Find her in two days, no matter what.

702
00:50:19,516 --> 00:50:20,809
How did it go?

703
00:50:23,270 --> 00:50:24,186
Unbelievable.

704
00:50:24,187 --> 00:50:27,691
There really was a guy named
Gwak Chi-hyeon in that department.

705
00:50:28,942 --> 00:50:30,360
And… Take a seat.

706
00:50:34,448 --> 00:50:36,365
My friend gave me his number.

707
00:50:36,366 --> 00:50:37,534
So,

708
00:50:38,076 --> 00:50:39,870
do you want to find out

709
00:50:41,038 --> 00:50:42,039
if your memory is real?

710
00:50:46,793 --> 00:50:48,795
SEOUN UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

711
00:50:53,300 --> 00:50:54,593
Please, can you stop…

712
00:50:56,094 --> 00:50:58,013
Can you please stop tailing me?

713
00:50:58,722 --> 00:51:02,225
I got fired from my job as an aide.
What could I do in this state…

714
00:51:10,609 --> 00:51:12,526
- Hello?
<i>- Is this Mr. Gwak Chi-hyeon?</i>

715
00:51:12,527 --> 00:51:13,569
Yes, it is.

716
00:51:13,570 --> 00:51:15,905
<i>This is Go Ji-won.</i>

717
00:51:15,906 --> 00:51:16,907
Ji-won?

718
00:51:18,158 --> 00:51:19,784
<i>Hey, Ji-won.</i>

719
00:51:19,785 --> 00:51:20,868
<i>Where are you?</i>

720
00:51:20,869 --> 00:51:24,164
Why haven't you been answering my calls?
Where are you?

721
00:51:27,459 --> 00:51:29,294
I'll explain the details

722
00:51:30,212 --> 00:51:31,171
in person.

723
00:51:31,838 --> 00:51:33,798
Sure. Where should we meet?

724
00:51:33,799 --> 00:51:34,841
<i>Where would be good?</i>

725
00:51:35,425 --> 00:51:36,468
In Seoul.

726
00:51:38,720 --> 00:51:41,305
Tonight, in Seoul.

727
00:51:41,306 --> 00:51:43,433
<i>Okay, let's do that. All right.</i>

728
00:51:46,812 --> 00:51:48,395
A clinic in Seoul?

729
00:51:48,396 --> 00:51:49,313
Yeah.

730
00:51:49,314 --> 00:51:53,692
Since some of her memory has returned,
I thought we could give it a boost

731
00:51:53,693 --> 00:51:56,862
by trying
a more sophisticated form of TMS.

732
00:51:56,863 --> 00:51:58,364
My friend runs a clinic,

733
00:51:58,365 --> 00:52:01,242
and they recently bought
an upgraded TMS machine.

734
00:52:01,243 --> 00:52:02,535
Of course we should go.

735
00:52:02,536 --> 00:52:03,870
When can we go?

736
00:52:04,746 --> 00:52:05,580
Tonight.

737
00:52:06,248 --> 00:52:07,998
- Tonight?
- Yeah.

738
00:52:07,999 --> 00:52:12,170
They're fully booked for a while,
so today is the only open slot.

739
00:52:13,130 --> 00:52:14,214
Let's go.

740
00:52:17,551 --> 00:52:19,844
But you have a lesson tonight.

741
00:52:19,845 --> 00:52:21,595
I can just reschedule it.

742
00:52:21,596 --> 00:52:25,307
I just happen to have a seminar
in Seoul today.

743
00:52:25,308 --> 00:52:28,060
I'm going to Seoul,
so I can take Ms. Go with me.

744
00:52:28,061 --> 00:52:30,105
- No need to go out of your way.
- It's fine.

745
00:52:31,398 --> 00:52:32,399
One second.

746
00:52:35,777 --> 00:52:37,236
Why is she calling me?

747
00:52:37,237 --> 00:52:38,446
KIM SONG-WOL

748
00:52:40,073 --> 00:52:40,907
Yes?

749
00:52:47,622 --> 00:52:49,040
Grandma!

750
00:52:50,208 --> 00:52:52,252
Grandma!

751
00:52:52,752 --> 00:52:54,420
- Ma'am?
- What's wrong?

752
00:52:54,421 --> 00:52:56,298
Grandma, what's wrong? What is it?

753
00:52:56,798 --> 00:52:57,674
What?

754
00:53:04,014 --> 00:53:07,142
DEPARTMENT OF NUCLEAR MEDICINE
PET-CT SCAN ROOM

755
00:53:29,122 --> 00:53:30,332
<i>She has a tumor.</i>

756
00:53:31,958 --> 00:53:33,375
If it's malignant,

757
00:53:33,376 --> 00:53:35,794
can she get surgery like last time?

758
00:53:35,795 --> 00:53:40,800
Well, her body is much weaker
than it was 14 years ago,

759
00:53:41,635 --> 00:53:43,303
so it would be more complicated.

760
00:53:44,471 --> 00:53:47,766
Let's wait for the test results first.

761
00:53:50,352 --> 00:53:51,186
Okay.

762
00:54:08,536 --> 00:54:10,871
I think I should stay with Grandma today.

763
00:54:10,872 --> 00:54:12,832
You should go to Seoul with Gi-jun.

764
00:54:13,708 --> 00:54:15,835
No, I'll go next time.

765
00:54:16,878 --> 00:54:19,547
You should go. Today's your only chance.

766
00:54:20,465 --> 00:54:23,676
Your treatment
is as important to me as Grandma.

767
00:54:23,677 --> 00:54:25,512
Grandma would want that too.

768
00:54:42,362 --> 00:54:44,114
- Thanks.
- It's nothing.

769
00:54:45,699 --> 00:54:47,993
These are your meds. Take them on time.

770
00:54:50,870 --> 00:54:51,829
I'll be back.

771
00:54:51,830 --> 00:54:53,831
Wait. Can you wait just a little?

772
00:54:53,832 --> 00:54:55,082
Mr. Hong's coming.

773
00:54:55,083 --> 00:54:55,959
What?

774
00:54:57,502 --> 00:54:58,836
Why is he coming?

775
00:54:58,837 --> 00:55:00,462
I asked him to go with you.

776
00:55:00,463 --> 00:55:03,882
You have your seminar.
Someone should take care of Eun-sae.

777
00:55:03,883 --> 00:55:06,719
There's no need.
I don't want to go with a stranger, okay?

778
00:55:06,720 --> 00:55:08,680
- We'll be fine.
- Yes.

779
00:55:09,264 --> 00:55:12,475
I don't want Mr. Hong
rescheduling his lessons for me.

780
00:55:13,101 --> 00:55:15,602
- Still…
- I won't leave her alone.

781
00:55:15,603 --> 00:55:17,397
Don't worry. See you when we get back.

782
00:55:20,275 --> 00:55:22,235
Hey, Gi-jun.

783
00:55:23,445 --> 00:55:24,404
Yes, Doctor?

784
00:55:24,904 --> 00:55:25,989
Has my grandma woken up?

785
00:55:44,090 --> 00:55:46,633
<i>This is Go Ji-won.</i>

786
00:55:46,634 --> 00:55:47,760
<i>Ji-won?</i>

787
00:55:47,761 --> 00:55:49,386
<i>Hey, Ji-won.</i>

788
00:55:49,387 --> 00:55:51,972
<i>Where are you?
Why haven't you been answering my calls?</i>

789
00:55:51,973 --> 00:55:53,600
<i>I'll explain the details</i>

790
00:55:54,476 --> 00:55:56,144
<i>in person.</i>

791
00:56:11,618 --> 00:56:12,744
Let's say

792
00:56:13,370 --> 00:56:18,124
this man called Gwak Chi-hyeon
really is your boyfriend.

793
00:56:18,708 --> 00:56:19,584
What then?

794
00:56:23,588 --> 00:56:25,464
If that's the case,

795
00:56:25,465 --> 00:56:28,343
it would be one of two things.

796
00:56:28,843 --> 00:56:32,180
Either Jang Tae-ha's fake,
or I was two-timing.

797
00:56:34,307 --> 00:56:35,642
Whatever the case,

798
00:56:36,434 --> 00:56:38,436
I think I'll be really sad.

799
00:56:59,624 --> 00:57:00,458
Grandma.

800
00:57:01,251 --> 00:57:02,085
Yeah?

801
00:57:03,336 --> 00:57:04,170
What?

802
00:57:05,088 --> 00:57:05,922
Are you okay?

803
00:57:09,050 --> 00:57:11,845
Am I… sick?

804
00:57:15,932 --> 00:57:17,100
We don't know yet.

805
00:57:17,934 --> 00:57:20,060
We have to wait for the test results.

806
00:57:20,061 --> 00:57:21,729
Don't you worry.

807
00:57:22,439 --> 00:57:24,607
I won't die that easily.

808
00:57:25,567 --> 00:57:30,029
After everything you did to save my life,
how could I possibly…

809
00:57:31,823 --> 00:57:36,953
I'm going to hold on tight and protect it.

810
00:57:39,706 --> 00:57:40,789
You promise?

811
00:57:40,790 --> 00:57:42,542
Yes, of course.

812
00:57:48,298 --> 00:57:51,551
Don't you know how strong I am?

813
00:57:53,928 --> 00:57:57,682
No matter how hard the disease
tries to get me,

814
00:57:58,641 --> 00:58:00,768
it won't stand a chance against me.

815
00:58:01,269 --> 00:58:02,395
No way.

816
00:58:15,617 --> 00:58:17,202
My precious baby.

817
00:58:19,704 --> 00:58:21,206
My absolute blessing.

818
00:58:27,629 --> 00:58:29,339
I'm going to be fine.

819
00:58:30,340 --> 00:58:33,760
You should go home and sleep comfortably.

820
00:58:34,802 --> 00:58:36,012
Okay?

821
00:58:38,932 --> 00:58:39,891
Go on home.

822
00:58:41,100 --> 00:58:41,935
Go on.

823
00:58:43,686 --> 00:58:46,021
I'm going to get some sleep.

824
00:58:46,022 --> 00:58:47,190
Go on home.

825
00:59:32,610 --> 00:59:35,113
BODEUM HOSPITAL CANCER CENTER

826
01:00:13,276 --> 01:00:14,152
Go Eun-sae.

827
01:00:14,861 --> 01:00:15,695
You…

828
01:00:16,195 --> 01:00:17,947
What happened to you?

829
01:00:19,032 --> 01:00:20,074
What about the treatment?

830
01:00:30,627 --> 01:00:31,628
Time for my meds.

831
01:00:41,012 --> 01:00:44,766
<i>In the middle of winter,
we were often kicked out barefoot.</i>

832
01:00:45,266 --> 01:00:49,395
Just thinking about
how the cold crept into my feet…

833
01:00:50,271 --> 01:00:51,606
<i>It still gives me the chills.</i>

834
01:01:08,623 --> 01:01:12,835
<i>Turns out MP3 players are still around.
Listen to this if you get carsick.</i>

835
01:01:14,212 --> 01:01:17,714
"Oh, I wish I could find
a discarded MP3 player or something."

836
01:01:17,715 --> 01:01:22,386
"Then I could listen to my favorite
god songs to help me get through it."

837
01:01:22,387 --> 01:01:25,014
<i>Those things were a luxury
for kids like me.</i>

838
01:01:27,016 --> 01:01:29,268
01. GOD - ONE CANDLE
02. GOD - LOVE YOU AND…

839
01:01:30,603 --> 01:01:32,355
Jang Tae-ha, you…

840
01:01:36,484 --> 01:01:38,361
What's wrong? Did you remember something?

841
01:01:41,072 --> 01:01:41,906
What the…

842
01:01:43,574 --> 01:01:45,535
Right, rain's forecast nationwide tonight.

843
01:01:47,829 --> 01:01:49,247
Doctor,

844
01:01:49,747 --> 01:01:51,081
let's just go back.

845
01:01:51,082 --> 01:01:52,125
What?

846
01:01:55,420 --> 01:01:57,296
I need to go back.

847
01:01:57,922 --> 01:01:59,339
What are you talking about?

848
01:01:59,340 --> 01:02:01,968
You're just going back
without even checking the facts?

849
01:02:04,762 --> 01:02:06,973
This can't be fake.

850
01:02:09,600 --> 01:02:11,602
Jang Tae-ha is real.

851
01:02:12,687 --> 01:02:14,731
So let's just go back.

852
01:02:17,734 --> 01:02:20,570
I want to go to Tae-ha right now.

853
01:02:27,368 --> 01:02:30,329
I asked about your treatment.
Did you get it already?

854
01:02:33,291 --> 01:02:35,126
If I said that I was more worried about

855
01:02:36,794 --> 01:02:39,464
you getting caught in the rain
than recovering my memory…

856
01:02:42,717 --> 01:02:43,801
would you believe me?

857
01:02:46,220 --> 01:02:48,181
Even if I can't do much else for you,

858
01:02:48,765 --> 01:02:50,975
on hard days like tonight,

859
01:02:52,935 --> 01:02:55,938
I thought I could at least shield you
from the rain.

860
01:02:58,775 --> 01:03:00,568
I really wanted to do that for you.

861
01:03:04,071 --> 01:03:05,822
<i>In my bleakest moments,</i>

862
01:03:05,823 --> 01:03:08,950
there was nothing
to shield me from the rain.

863
01:03:08,951 --> 01:03:11,788
It felt like a reminder
of just how hopeless things were.

864
01:03:12,288 --> 01:03:13,247
So I don't like rain.

865
01:03:22,715 --> 01:03:24,509
Let's weather it together from now on.

866
01:03:29,138 --> 01:03:30,765
I'll be with you.

867
01:04:36,831 --> 01:04:38,499
OUR STICKY LOVE

868
01:05:25,129 --> 01:05:29,091
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
